INSERT INTO `price_faq` VALUES (13,2,'What else can affect the price?','<p>Obviously, we are unable to display all possible scenarios of work in this calculator. We showed only those that are more common and frequently encountered in our everyday work. The calculator was created in order to get acquainted with our pricing, nothing more. There are many more different factors that can affect the evaluation and either increase or decrease the price. Our goal in the discussion process of the project is to reach compromise and find the best possible solutions. We are always glad to get acquainted with you, even if you do not have a specific task for us at the moment and you just want to get to know our service better. Please, feel free to write or call us. We will be glad to communicate with you.</p>'),(14,3,'What is included in the price of the project?','<p>The cost of the project includes all 5 stages of production. From the initial angle selection and up to the final renders. Additional changes after the final render, depending on their scope and quantity, can be subject to additional fees. The additional fees are negotiable and we do our best to accommodate all details during the main stages of production.<br />While making this price calculator we evaluated the pictures in 5000px size. In case if you require a different size of pictures for your project - this is not a problem for us, just please let us know about this beforehand.<br />Usually, the price does not include the transfer of source files and lifetime NDA, so if this is important for you, please let us know before the start of the project. Our price includes an NDA of 2 months for each project. The price also does not include purchasing expensive content on stocks, therefore it is important to discuss such kind of details at the initial stage of the project.</p>'),(15,1,'Interior complexity','<p>Here are the most common factors that are taken into consideration while evaluating the project complexity:</p>\n<p>- complexity of the interior design<br />- camera angle complexity<br />- size of the room<br />- number of details<br />- possibility to use library content or a requirement to model furniture from scratch<br />- number and type of people on the pictures (2D/3D)<br />- size of the picture<br />- number of camera angles in one room<br />- our role in working on this project (taking part in creating the design or working according to the technical task)<br />- timeframes of the project</p>\n<p>These are only several of the main things that we take into account while evaluating the project and now you are aware of our price range and our evaluation strategy. Nevertheless, the best solution would be to send us your project for evaluation so we could examine it and present you the options and solutions that we can offer depending on your requirements and technical task information.</p>'),(16,0,'Exterior complexity','<p>Here are the most common factors that are taken into consideration while evaluating the project complexity:</p>\n<p>- complexity of the architecture<br />- environment<br />- camera angle complexity<br />- making the picture in full 3d or photomontage<br />- time of the day<br />- season<br />- size of the picture<br />- whether the client has a 3d model of the building<br />- number and type of people on the pictures (2D/3D)<br />- timeframes of the project</p>\n<p>These are only several of the main things that we take into account while evaluating the project and now you are aware of our price range and our evaluation strategy. Nevertheless, the best solution would be to send us your project for evaluation so we could examine it and present you the options and solutions that we can offer depending on your requirements and technical task information.</p>');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `price_faq` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

